# Git & commits — fieldops-app

This repository is the Expo consuming app only. Commit messages refer to app concerns — not library publish internals.

## Format — Conventional Commits

`type(scope): summary` — imperative mood, no trailing period, ≤72 character summary line.

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `test`, `docs`, `chore`, `build`, `ci`, `style`, `perf`.

Scopes (examples):
- `feat(core): add theme tokens`
- `feat(integrations): add query provider port`
- `feat(work-orders): add list ViewModel`
- `feat(router): wire QueryProvider`
- `docs(decisions): record 409 conflict UX`
- `chore(cursor): add architecture rules`

Body (optional) explains **why**. Point lasting trade-offs at `DECISIONS.md`.

Breaking changes use `!` when intentional.

## Granularity

- One logical change per commit. Revertable without breaking the build.
- Sequence: scaffold → theme/config → integrations → router/providers → feature slices → tests → docs.
- Config / dependency / lockfile changes get their own `chore:` / `build:` commit when heavy — especially new vendors behind integrations.
- Never leave `wip` or `fixes` as the final message of finished work.
- Formatting-only changes are their own `style:` commit.
- No secrets, committed `.env` files, or machine-local ports.

## History hygiene

- Prefer small commits that show dependency isolation (integration adapter before features call it).
- After a shared or reviewed push, do not rewrite history. Local rebase before final handoff is fine for a solo submission.
- Commit and push only when the human asks — except an explicit foundation/implementation plan that requires commit+push per layer.
